{#- _mascot.html.j2 — the site's mascot (owner decision 2026-10-13: a small yellow chick with a blue scarf and a brown
    backpack, soft 3D clay, only on this site). It appears only in guide spots — the launcher, the question box of the
    home, and later the chat states, empty results, 404 and help; scenery and banners stay the gouache illustrations.
    Always decorative: alt="" — the words beside it say what the spot is for. {% import "_mascot.html.j2" as mm %}

    pic(name, kind, show, cls): a <picture> of templates/assets/mascot/<name>-<px>.avif|webp (tools/mascot_media.py
    makes them square, so width = height = show, the size the page draws it at, and it has its room from the first
    paint): AVIF first, WebP after, the kind's 1× and 2× files — icon 64·128, small 96·192, medium 200·400
    (MASCOT_PX = tools/mascot_media.py SIZES; tests/test_mascot.py checks that every file a page names exists).
    fetchpriority low: it never takes bandwidth from a page's first picture. -#}
{% set MASCOT_PX = {'icon': (64, 128), 'small': (96, 192), 'medium': (200, 400)} %}
{% macro pic(name, kind, show, cls='') -%}
{%- set px = MASCOT_PX[kind] -%}
{%- set base = '/assets/mascot/' ~ name ~ '-' -%}
<picture{% if cls %} class="{{ cls }}"{% endif %}><source type="image/avif" srcset="{{ base }}{{ px[0] }}.avif 1x, {{ base }}{{ px[1] }}.avif 2x"><img src="{{ base }}{{ px[0] }}.webp" srcset="{{ base }}{{ px[0] }}.webp 1x, {{ base }}{{ px[1] }}.webp 2x" width="{{ show }}" height="{{ show }}" alt="" decoding="async" fetchpriority="low"></picture>
{%- endmacro %}
